<Barack_Obama> <media_common.quotation_subject.quotations_about_this_subject> "“What we do today does not always secure reasonable hope for tomorrow. Only this time––with the fact of Barack Obama’s presidential nomination––our country had overcome the odds in a profoundly miraculous way. Like millions––literally, millions––of others, I was privileged to bear witness to a gift of history more than 200 years in the making: it was and it is a moment worthy of joy’s sweet and bitter tears. ” from blog Why I Cried When Barack Obama Received the Democratic Nomination for President of the United States" .
